WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.040
- Alright, we've hit that time in the show

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.840
where I share something cool from

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.250
the pages of social media, this is

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.410
what I'm liking.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.243
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:09.090
(audience cheering)

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.030
- 'Tis the season for ghost
stories and total spookiness

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.710
and one New York artist is bringing

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.410
the craziest tales of hauntings to life

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.840
with a series she calls "Inktober"

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.171
It's something she's been doing since 2018

00:00:21.171 --> 00:00:23.200
and she turns them into books.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.781
Everybody, let's say hi
to Jessica watching on NBC

00:00:25.781 --> 00:00:27.018
for New York at three.

00:00:27.018 --> 00:00:28.586
What's up Jessica?

00:00:28.586 --> 00:00:30.390
(crowd cheers)

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.467
- Hi, how are you?

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.000
- [Kelly] I'm so good,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.890
so how did you come up with this idea

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.470
- So, I've always had a
love for ghost stories

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.690
and all things spooky
and the series started

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.910
as a way for my to build my art portfolio

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.140
and I thought it would be really cool

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.240
to focus on folklore
from around the world.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.280
And I basically started by doing a bunch

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.260
of research do a sketch based on

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.230
the story and then I'll head
into the inking process.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.330
Um, I try to incorporate elements from

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.590
the story as I can

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.568
whether it's the clothing
from that time period

00:00:57.568 --> 00:01:00.270
or sometimes if there's
an animal in the story

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.790
I'll include the skull or
the antlers of that animal.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.152
Um, and by the end of
this month I'll have done

00:01:05.152 --> 00:01:06.367
90 stories so far.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.200
(audiences applauds)

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.350
- You are so incredibly gifted, my gosh.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.540
It's so beautiful, so cool.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.580
Um, we're looking at video of you creating

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.080
one of your favorites, so tell us

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.760
about the Lady From Boston.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.080
- [Jessica] So, the Lady In Black

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.480
tells the tale of Melanie Lanier

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.670
and her husband was being kept prisoner

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.400
in Fort Warren in Boston Massachusetts.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.380
So, she came up with a plan to free him

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.353
using a pickax to tunnel
through the prison

00:01:30.353 --> 00:01:32.670
and unfortunately they were captured

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.680
and sentenced to death and it's said

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.652
that today her ghost still roams that area

00:01:36.652 --> 00:01:39.091
and holding on to the
guilt of what happened.

00:01:39.091 --> 00:01:41.353
And I thought the story
was just sorta tragic

00:01:41.353 --> 00:01:43.277
so with my art I always try to combine

00:01:43.277 --> 00:01:46.230
the creepy with the beautiful and a lot

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.790
of the responses to
the story have actually

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.890
been people who are
planning a trip to Boston

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.660
and now they get really excited that they

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.570
have a piece of spooky history
to bring with them now.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:56.610
- [Kelly] Yeah, oh my gosh,
what an intense story.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.311
Well, thank you so much Jessica.

00:01:58.311 --> 00:01:59.144
(crowd applauds)

00:01:59.144 --> 00:02:00.136
- [Kelly] I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:00.136 --> 00:02:00.969
- [Jessica] Thank you

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:01.802
(bell rings)

00:02:01.802 --> 00:02:03.420
oh, thank you so much

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.280
- And that's not all
our season long partner

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.960
Pilot Pen Makers of Frixion the go-to,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.880
erasable pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.740
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.688
just like you ma'am, so
they're giving you $1,000.

00:02:12.688 --> 00:02:13.521
How's that sound?

00:02:13.521 --> 00:02:15.169
(crowd cheers and applauds)

00:02:15.169 --> 00:02:17.543
- Oh my gosh, thank you so much.

00:02:17.543 --> 00:02:20.130
- [Kelly] Absolutely, keep
up all the inspiration

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:20.963
it's so creative.

00:02:20.963 --> 00:02:22.950
Thank you so much and thank you to all

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.010
our guests this hour,
Josh Duhamel, Sosie Bacon,

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:29.340
Antonia Lafaso, Nate Arena, Chad and JT

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.033
All the great day, if it's
not well try and change it.

